Pushed. Here's what was fixed:

**Root cause:** The committed code on the branch had 4 real TypeScript errors that caused `npx tsc --noEmit` to fail in CI:

1. **`app/(tabs)/index.tsx:234`** — `.map(demoChargeToStripRow)` passed a function with an optional 2nd arg `options?`, but `Array.map` passes `(value, index, array)` — the `index: number` was incompatible with `options?: { showAccountIndicator?: boolean }`. Fixed by wrapping: `.map((tx) => demoChargeToStripRow(tx))`

2. **`app/(tabs)/shared/index.tsx:531-532`** — `a.balances.length` and `b.balances.length` accessed on a possibly-undefined field. Fixed with `(a.balances ?? []).length`

3. **`app/_layout.tsx:242`** — `apiFetch` was typed as `(path, opts?: RequestInit)` in `ProTierProvider`, but the actual function passed from `_layout.tsx` uses `Omit<RequestInit, "body"> & { body?: object | FormData }`. Fixed by updating the type signature in `lib/pro-tier-context.tsx` to match.

Tests (7/7) and Expo config validation both pass locally.
